From a7db735c68e12d5baedbe8a84ed9178b0d66040d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:24:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] Gather the Fourier-response stack into
 equicdft.response

response/modes.py (wavevector indices, probe directions and validation,
from _fourier.py), response/curvature.py (the symmetric finite-difference
curvatures, from _fourier.py), response/response.py (FourierResponse, from
response.py; re-exported by the package so equicdft.response keeps its
meaning), response/stability.py (FourierStabilityLoss, with a deprecated
shim at equicdft.stability), and the three classes that lived beside
training code: response/loss.py (FourierResponseLoss, from loss.py),
response/metrics.py (FourierResponseMetrics, from metrics.py) and
response/data.py (FourierResponseData, from data.py). The old homes of
those three classes re-export them again once loss/metrics move to
equicdft.training and data becomes a package in the next two commits.
Golden outputs unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
